  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3226.26 Brake Lining, Pad Wear and Service Brake Systems",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3226.26 Brake Lining, Pad Wear and Service Brake Systems.\n\n(a) A vehicle shall be rejected for brake lining or pad wear if:\n\n(1) The vehicle has a gross vehicle weight rating of 10,000 pounds or less and bonded linings are less than 2/32 inch at their thinnest point;\n\n(2) The vehicle has a gross vehicle weight rating of 10,000 pounds or less and riveted linings are less than 2/32 inch above any rivet head at the thinnest point;\n\n(3) The vehicle has a gross vehicle weight rating in excess of 10,000 pounds and has:\n\na. Air drum brakes that are less than 6/32 inch (3/16 inch) at the shoe center for a shoe with a continuous strip of lining;\n\nb. Air drum brakes that are less than 8/32 inch (1/4 inch) at the shoe center for a shoe with two pads;\n\nc. Air brakes that are less than 8/32 inch (1/4 inch) at the shoe center;\n\nd. Air drum brakes that are worn to the wear indicator if the lining is so marked;\n\ne. Air disc brakes that are less than 4/32 inch (1/8 inch);\n\nf. Hydraulic disc and drum brakes that are less than 2/32 inch (1/16 inch) measured at the shoe center; or\n\ng. Electric disc and drum brakes that are less than 2/32 inch (1/16 inch) measured at the shoe center; or\n\n(4) The wire in wire-backed linings is visible on the friction surface.\n\n(b) A vehicle shall be rejected if the service brake chambers are:\n\n(1) Mismatched on any axle, or\n\n(2) Air chamber mounting devices are loose, broken, cracked or missing.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16; ss by #12932, eff 11-27-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
}
